depletion a risk

965
01:08:30,290 --> 01:08:33,050
factor for
acetaminophen toxicity?

966
01:08:35,450 --> 01:08:38,930
Acetaminophen undergoes
saturable metabolism via

967
01:08:38,930 --> 01:08:43,210
glucuronidation, sulfation,
and oxidation via CYPs.

968
01:08:43,890 --> 01:08:49,950
CYP2E1 generates NAPQI, an
unstable toxic intermediate,

969
01:08:49,950 --> 01:08:53,910
which is detoxified by
glutathione S-transferase

970
01:08:53,910 --> 01:08:59,170
to a non-toxic water
-soluble metabolite. If

971
01:08:59,170 --> 01:09:01,890
glutathione levels are
reduced because of genetic or

972
01:09:01,890 --> 01:09:05,830
acquired deficiency, an
APQI may accumulate, leading

973
01:09:05,830 --> 01:09:08,690
to oxidative stress,
mitochondrial dysfunction,

974
01:09:09,110 --> 01:09:12,010
adduct formation, in
other words binding

975
01:09:12,010 --> 01:09:16,790
actually to cellular
macromolecules, and

976
01:09:16,790 --> 01:09:20,110
And that can lead to
hepatocyte necrosis.

